  "name": "Late-revealed lane debris",
  "description": "A stationary debris object is absent during the initial approach and appears in the ego lane only after the ego has committed to the road. A roadside box truck near the approach provides a plausible late visual reveal without being declared as a guaranteed occlusion. The debris is placed on the same reference lane with enough longitudinal room for a firm but survivable response.",
